  {
    "title": "Some characters have more than one reading",
    "body": "A few common characters change their sound with their meaning: 觉 is jué in 觉得 but jiào in 睡觉; 长 is cháng (long) or zhǎng (to grow); 还 is hái (still) or huán (to give back); 了 is le or liǎo. Learn them with the word.",
    "pattern": "[了的得地着还行长重觉都好为乐]",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "觉得 (juéde)",
        "say": "JÜEH-duh, rising + neutral",
        "en": "to feel, to think"
      },
      {
        "word": "睡觉 (shuìjiào)",
        "say": "shway-JYOW, falling + falling",
        "en": "to sleep"
      },
      {
        "word": "长 (cháng)",
        "say": "chahng, rising",
        "en": "long"
      },
      {
        "word": "长大 (zhǎngdà)",
        "say": "jahng-DAH, low + falling",
        "en": "to grow up"
      }
    ]
  },
